<title>ESTONIA: UHISPANK CONVERTS PEP SHARES.</title>
<headline>UHISPANK CONVERTS PEP SHARES.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uhispank said on Monday that it will convert the remaining former Pohja-Eesti Pank (PEP) shares into Uhispank shares on May 26.</p>
<p>In a statement, the bank said that according to a decision of the general meeting held in April, 500,000 PEP shares with a nominal value of 100 kroons will be converted into five million Uhispank shares with a nominal value of 10 kroons.</p>
<p>Trading in the new shares will happen after the share conversion has been registered in the company register, the statement added.</p>
<p>The two banks signed a merger agreement in January this year and the agreement was approved by their annual general meeting in April.</p>
<p>-- David Mardiste, Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
